e downloaded file: 7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732\nLocation: 35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8 (confidence medium)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#preamble-op1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"=== PDF page 7 of 96 ===\nTHE PRESIDENT 2857\nExecutive Order T1509\nESTABLISHING THE PRESIDENT’S ADVISORY COUNCIL ON  \nMANAGEMENT IMPROVEMENT\nW HEREAS finding ways in which, to improve management and \nefficiency in the executive branch meets a vital and continuing need ; \nand\nW HEREAS it is essential that the resources of the executive branch \nwhich are devoted, to the fulfillment of our international responsibili­\nties and the needs of our citizens be managed and utilized in as effective \n.  a manner as possible ; and\nW HEREAS the best management practices and techniques de- \n-veloped by individual Government agencies and by business and in­\ndustry should be utilized in .  all Government agencies whenever \napplicable; and\nW HEREAS there is a need to review the progress of the Govern­\nment’ s management improvement program and to furnish the Presi­\ndent advice thereon ; and\nW HEREAS it is desirable to give increased attention to the im­\nprovement of the management of executive agencies and programs :\nNOW,-THEREFORE, by virtue of the authority vested in me as \nPresident of the United States, it is ordered as follows ;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; operative words before the numbered sections","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#preamble-op2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) There is hereby es­\ntablished the President’ s Advisory Council on Management Improve­\nment (hereinafter referred to as the Council).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 1(a)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec1(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) *  The Council shall be composed of 10 members, all „of whom \nshall be appointed by the President from among citizens outside the \nGovernment and who shall serve at the pleasure of the President. \nThe President shall designate one of the members of the Council to \nserve as Chairman.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 1(b)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec1(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Each member of the Council shall be entitled to receive com­\npensation for each day he is engaged on business of the Council, and \ntravel expenses, including per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized \nby law (5 U.S.C. 3109 and 5703) for persons in the Government service \nemployed intermittently.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 1(c)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec1(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Functions o f the Council.  As requested-by the President or \nthe Director of the Bureau of the Budget, the Council shall, from \ntime to time :","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Provide advice and assistance on Government-wide and inter­\nagency management problems.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Make systematic appraisals of Government-wide operations \nto identify opportunities to improve efficiency and cost control.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Carry forward the functions which were vested in the Presi­\ndent’ s Advisory Council on Cost Reduction by Executive Order \nNo. 11353 of May 23,1967, as amended, but without regard to the time \nlimitation contained therein.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) Provide for an interchange of ideas with responsible operating \nofficials throughout the executive branch on opportunities for manage­\nment improvement and appropriate action to achieve such \nimprovement.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2(d)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(e) Submit reports to the President containing appropriate \nrecommendations for improving the efficiency of Government-wide \noperations.\nFEDERAL REGISTER, V O L 35, NO. 30— THURSDAY, FEBRUARY 12, 1970\n\n=== PDF page 8 of 96 ===\n2858 THE PRESIDENT\nSec. 3. Assistance by Federal agencies.  The Office of Executive \nManagement, Bureau of the Budget, shall provide staff assistance to \nthe Council and, upon request of the Chairman of the Council, other \n-executive departments and agencies shall, consistent with law, furnish \nto the Council available information which the Council may require \nin performance of its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 2(e)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec2(e)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Sawing provision.  Nothing in this order shall derogate from \nthe functions or status of the President’ s Advisory Council on Execu­\ntive Organization established by the President on April 5, 1969.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 4","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"S ec. 5. P rior order. Without prejudice to the provisions of section \n2(c) hereof, the following are hereby revoked:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 5 (lead-in)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec5","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(1) Executive Order \nNo. 11353 of May 23, 1967, and (2) Executive Order. No. 11418 of \nJuly 27,1968. -","original_source":{"page_or_item":"35 FR 2857, PDF pages 7-8; Sec. 5(1)","sha256":"7a118460eb74a8b96a5e915874d2166a8d799dbb282c4f059144114e35019732","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1970-02-12/pdf/FR-1970-02-12.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:11509#sec5(1)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":null,"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: original_representation not yet confirmed","DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 14 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id"